body:
I am generally following the [Example 4](https://wicg.github.io/serial/#readable-example) to read serial port line by line. I want to rely on `AbortController` to close the serial port. However, I'm getting `Uncaught (in promise) TypeError: Failed to execute 'close' on 'SerialPort': Cannot cancel a locked stream` when calling `abortController.abort()`even if I passed the abort signal to `.pipeThrough`. After debugging, it seems that upstreams of the pipe are still locked and I'm not able to `.cancel` since it will throw `AbortError`. What is the proper way to handle this?

I've seen similar issues 
- https://github.com/WICG/serial/issues/112 (Calling `.cancel` will throw `AbortError`)
- https://stackoverflow.com/questions/71262432/how-can-i-close-a-web-serial-port-that-ive-piped-through-a-transformstream (Uses `.pipeTo`)


```ts
serialPort
  .open(serialOptions)
  .then(async () => {
    if (!serialPort.readable) {
      throw new Error(
        "No readable stream after opening serial port successfully"
      );
    }

    const textDecoderStream = new TextDecoderStream();
    const transformStream = new TransformStream<string, string>(
      new LineBreakTransformer()
    );

    const lineStream = serialPort.readable
      .pipeThrough(textDecoderStream, {
        signal: abortSignal,
      })
      .pipeThrough(transformStream, { signal: abortSignal });

    try {
      for await (const line of readStream(lineStream)) {
        setLines((prev) => [
          ...prev.slice(-1000),
          {
            content: line,
            timestamp: new Date(),
          },
        ]);
      }
    } finally {
      console.warn(serialPort.readable.locked);  // expect false, got true
      console.warn(textDecoderStream.writable.locked);  // expect false, got true
      console.warn(textDecoderStream.readable.locked);  // expect false, got true
      console.warn(transformStream.writable.locked);  // expect false, got true
      console.warn(transformStream.readable.locked);  // expect false, got false
      console.warn(lineStream.locked);  // expect false, got false
    }
  })
  .catch((err: Error) => abortSignal.aborted || setError(err))
  .finally(() => serialPort.close());  // Uncaught (in promise) TypeError: Failed to execute 'close' on 'SerialPort': Cannot cancel a locked stream
```

```ts
async function* readStream<T>(stream: ReadableStream<T>): AsyncGenerator<T> {
  const reader = stream.getReader();

  try {
    while (true) {
      const { done, value } = await reader.read();

      if (done) {
        break;
      }

      yield value;
    }
  } finally {
    reader.releaseLock();
  }
}

class LineBreakTransformer implements Transformer<string, string> {
  private container: string;

  constructor() {
    this.container = "";
  }

  transform(
    chunk: string,
    controller: TransformStreamDefaultController<string>
  ): void | PromiseLike<void> {
    this.container += chunk;
    const lines = this.container.split("\r\n");
    this.container = lines.pop() ?? "";
    lines.forEach((line) => controller.enqueue(line));
  }

  flush(
    controller: TransformStreamDefaultController<string>
  ): void | PromiseLike<void> {
    controller.enqueue(this.container);
  }
}
```
